    <static seed="1" source="Library/TCNJ/TCNJ_LinearSystems/problem1.pg">
      <statement><p>Determine whether the following system has no solution, an infinite number of solutions or a unique solution.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rllrrr}
-3 x \amp + 3 y \amp = \amp 9 \cr
-6 x \amp  - 5 y \amp = \amp 5 \cr
-9 x \amp  - 13 y \amp = \amp 1
\end{array} \right.</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rllrrr}
-3 x \amp + 3 y \amp = \amp 9 \cr
-6 x \amp  - 5 y \amp = \amp 5 \cr
-9 x \amp  - 13 y \amp = \amp -1
\end{array} \right.</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rllrrr}
-8 x \amp  - 8 y  \amp = \amp -16 \cr
-6 x \amp  - 6 y \amp = \amp -12 \cr
-14 x \amp  - 14 y \amp = \amp -28
\end{array} \right.</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    </static>
