  <webwork-reps version="2" webwork2_major_version="2" webwork2_minor_version="20" xml:id="extracted-webwork-3" ww-id="webwork-3">
    <static seed="3" source="Library/WHFreeman/Holt_linear_algebra/Chaps_1-4/holt_01_01_024.pg">
      <statement><p>Find the set of solutions for the linear system</p>
<p><me>\begin{array}{rcrcrcr} x_1  \amp  - \amp  2 x_{2} \amp  - \amp  3 x_{3} \amp  = \amp  6 \\ \amp  - \amp  x_{2} \amp  - \amp  4 x_{3} \amp  = \amp  -11 \\ \amp  \amp   \amp   \amp  4 x_{3} \amp  = \amp  8\end{array}</me> Use <alert>s1</alert>, <alert>s2</alert>, etc. for the free variables if necessary.</p>
<p><m>(x_1, x_2, x_3) = \bigg(</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>\bigg)</m></p>
</statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>18</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>3</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>2</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <solution><p><alert>SOLUTION:</alert>
Equation 3 <m>\Rightarrow x_3 = 2</m>. Substitute into equation 2, <m>-x_2  - 4(2) = -11 \Rightarrow x_2 = 3</m>. Substitute into equation 1, <m>x_1  - 2(3)  - 3(2) = 6 \Rightarrow x_1 = 18</m>.</p>
</solution>
