      <statement><p>Give a geometric description of the following systems of equations</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rrrrrr}\amp  15 \,x\amp - \amp 15 \,y\amp =\amp 15\\\amp  -6 \, x\amp +\amp  6 \, y\amp =\amp -6\\\amp  -21 \, x\amp +\amp  21 \, y\amp =\amp -21\\ \end{array}\right.</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rrrrrr}\amp   \,x\amp +\amp  3 \, y\amp =\amp 5\\\amp  4 \,x\amp +\amp  5 \, y\amp =\amp 9\\\amp  15 \,x\amp +\amp  17 \, y\amp =\amp 31\\ \end{array}\right.</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rrrrrr}\amp   \,x\amp +\amp  3 \, y\amp =\amp 5\\\amp  4 \,x\amp +\amp  5 \, y\amp =\amp 9\\\amp  15 \,x\amp +\amp  17 \, y\amp =\amp 30\\ \end{array}\right.</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
