    <static seed="5" source="Library/TCNJ/TCNJ_LinearSystems/problem4.pg">
      <statement><p>Give a geometric description of the following system of equations</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rrrrrrr}
2x \amp  + \amp  4y \amp  - \amp  6z \amp  = \amp  12 \cr
-x \amp  + \amp  5y \amp  - \amp  9z \amp  = \amp  1
\end{array} \right.</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rrrrrrr}
2x \amp  + \amp  4y \amp  - \amp  6z \amp  = \amp  12 \cr
-3x \amp  - \amp  6y \amp  + \amp  9z \amp  = \amp  16
\end{array}\right.</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lbrace\begin{array}{rrrrrrr}
2x \amp  + \amp  4y \amp  - \amp  6z \amp  = \amp  -12 \cr
-3x \amp  - \amp  6y \amp  + \amp  9z \amp  = \amp  18
\end{array} \right.</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
